      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Confidence calibration",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The agent incorrectly suggested lowering pe_004 from confident to probable. The existing confident tier is acceptable based on the agreement of the record's name, age, place, and household position. Since the task was to identify missing links rather than reassess confidence tiers, this recommendation was unnecessary and inconsistent with the expected calibration."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_person_evidence_w2t",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Confidence calibration",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The agent correctly recognized the impossible-event warning caused by the 1881 census conflicting with John Carter's existing 1870 burial. It appropriately refused to create a link and did not override or alter the existing tree fact. However, under the scenario's evaluation criteria, refusing the link and writing no person-evidence link is a partial result for confidence calibration. The agent should receive partial credit because it respected the conflict rather than forcing an identity match."
